From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: writeback bands, the collector's write-back without a fresh allocation (EDEN_UP_WRITEBACK_BANDS)

DRAFT, not built. Our own work (no upstream port), after waveydude's GPUBack std::bad_alloc in
SwizzleImage (a 32 MiB scratch grow with 4 to 8 MiB free). Gated by EDEN_UP_WRITEBACK_BANDS
(exact 1), a live switch (Id WritebackBands, armed: the kept buffer is malloc'd in the
TextureCache constructor only when it is 1 at boot); off by default. On: a block-linear
subresource whose guest range is not one host span is written back in bands of whole block rows
through the kept buffer (EDEN_UP_WRITEBACK_BANDS_MIB, 1 to 32, default 8); every case the bands
do not cover takes the old path. EDEN_UP_WRITEBACK_BANDS_VERIFY=1 (boot) also does each banded
write-back the old way and compares. EDEN_TEST_WRITEBACK_SPLIT=1 is a test aid. 10 s line while
on: "EDEN_UP_WRITEBACK_BANDS: wb=". The armed count comment goes from Eleven to Twelve.

Reviewed draft from the gc-scratch job, verdict "ready", no v2: the plain patch is used as
written; the reviewer corrected only README and test plan notes (keep L1028 off in verify runs,
warm pipelines for the starvation A/B) and noted that gc-writeback-skip should land with it.
